Rust libraries, linked into the program: names, versions and licences are in
licenses/licenses-rust.txt, written from Cargo.lock by scripts/licenses.py; their
texts and where their source is, in licenses/THIRD-PARTY-RUST.txt of each package.

Swift and its runtime libraries (https://swift.org, 6.4.3: the standard library,
Foundation, Dispatch), beside the program on Windows and inside oort-core on Linux:
Apache License 2.0 with Runtime Library Exception, in licenses/Swift-LICENSE.txt.
Foundation includes ICU, by Unicode, Inc. and others: licenses/ICU-LICENSE.txt.

Microsoft Visual C++ runtime libraries, beside the program on Windows, unchanged:
distributable code of Microsoft Visual Studio, under its licence terms.

WebView2, on Windows, is Microsoft's and is not part of this package: the loader
linked into the program is from the WebView2 SDK (licenses/WebView2-SDK-LICENSE.txt);
where WebView2 is missing, the installer fetches Microsoft's own installer.
The Windows installer is made with NSIS (https://nsis.sourceforge.io, zlib/libpng).

On Linux the window is WebKitGTK's. The .deb uses the system's; the AppImage carries
it, with GTK, GStreamer and the libraries they need, as separate files unchanged from
Debian 12 (LGPL, GPL and other licences): licenses/THIRD-PARTY-LINUX.txt of the
AppImage names each, with its licence and where the source of that version is.

No trademark owner named in catalog.json (game and console names, to say what a
project is for) is affiliated with Oort NX or endorses it.
